Erik Hesselink wrote on 10/05/2003 10:44 AM:
> Stanislav Traykov wrote:
[thrones]

> The tree of all posibilities looks like this:
> 
> First, there is a 2/3 chance of nothing happening. If nothing happens, 
> there's a 1/3 chance the throne disappears, and a 2/3 chance we go back 
> to the start.
> 
> If something happens, there's a 1/13 chance of a wish, a 1/13 chance of 
> teleport away (assuming TC) and an 11/13 chance of something else. If 
> you teleport away, go back to the start. If something else happens, 
> there's a 1/3 chance the throne disappears, and a 2/3 chance we go back 
> to the beginning.
> 
> The chance to go back to the beginning is 2/3(nothing)*2/3(doesn't 
> disappear) + 1/3(something)*1/13(teleport) + 
> 1/3(something)*11/13*2/3(doesn't disappear) = 77/117.
> 
> Now, the chance of a wish is 1/3(something)*1/13(wish) + 77/117(start 
> again)*1/3*1/13 + (77/117)^2(start again twice)*1/3*1/13 + ...
> 
> This is 1/39 (chance of a wish) times the sum of (77/117)^n with n from 
> 0 to infinity. This is a geometrical series, which converges to 
> 1/(1-77/117) = 117/40. So the chance of a wish is 1/39 * 117/40 = 3/40.
> 
> What did I miss?

